;;; A bare `_` as a fact's argument is dropped at load, in silence — M1f
;;; **W29**, register row `W29/fact-arg` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; banked by S1f.5.0 (2026-11-08) from S1f.5.1's case (the inventory of
;;; 2026-11-06's W-22; its probe `fact_wild_arg.ein` wrote `(r _ ?x)`, and the
;;; variable, G-6's, is written `a` here), filed `open` and owned by S1f.5.1,
;;; on the user's ruling of 2026-11-06 (Q-M1e2.22).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A relation of two arguments and two facts over it, the first writing the
;;; bare `_` as its first argument.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A bare `_` is reserved and names nothing (the user, 2026-11-06: *"simple
;;; `_` reserved and refused because of potential ambiguity"*), so the program
;;; is refused at load, with a line naming the place: every command that reads
;;; it exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The loader drops the `_` and stores the one-argument `(r a)` beside
;;; `(r a b)`, against a two-argument declaration, with no line (`ein saturate
;;; FILE --dump`). Root's state is `(model (r a b) (r a))` and R is two states,
;;; exit 0 (`ein solve FILE` and `ein oracle FILE` at `ec004a48`, the engine
;;; `916d97ac`'s, release and debug alike).

(relation r T T)
(r _ a)
(r a b)
